---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro'
import BlogPostShell from '../../components/BlogPostShell.astro'
import BlogToolEmbed from '../../components/BlogToolEmbed.astro'

const slug = 'luminance-converter'
const seo = {
  title: 'Nits to foot-lamberts converter — luminance | maratool',
  description: 'Convert cd/m² (nits), foot-lamberts, stilbs, and lamberts with NIST factors. Free browser luminance converter.',
  canonical: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}`,
  schema: {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BlogPosting',
    headline: 'How to convert nits to foot-lamberts (screen brightness)',
    image: 'https://maratool.com/og/converter.svg',
    datePublished: '2026-07-25',
    dateModified: '2026-07-25',
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Marcell Almeida', url: 'https://marcell.com.br' },
    publisher: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'maratool',
      url: 'https://maratool.com',
      logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://maratool.com/favicon.svg' },
    },
    mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}` },
    url: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}`,
    description: 'Convert cd/m² (nits), foot-lamberts, stilbs, and lamberts with NIST factors. Free browser luminance converter.',
  },
  breadcrumbSchema: {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://maratool.com' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://maratool.com/blog' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'How to convert nits to foot-lamberts (screen brightness)', item: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}` },
    ],
  },
}
---
<Base {...seo}>
  <Layout>
    <BlogPostShell
      title="How to convert nits to foot-lamberts (screen brightness)"
      lead="Type a luminance — read nits, fL, stilbs, or lamberts instantly."
      date="July 25, 2026"
      dateIso="2026-07-25"
    >
      <p>Display specs quote nits, projection standards quote foot-lamberts, and photometry texts use stilbs. The <a href="/luminance-converter">Luminance Converter</a> moves between them with exact π-based factors.</p>

      <BlogToolEmbed slug="luminance-converter" title="Try it — convert luminance units" height={440} />

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Pick units</strong> — "Candela per square meter / Nit (cd/m²)" to "Foot-lambert (fL)", or any other pair.</li>
        <li><strong>Type a value</strong> — the result updates as you type, with swap and copy.</li>
        <li><strong>Copy</strong> — one click, with "Copied!" feedback.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Luminance conversion factors</h2>
      <p>Every unit converts through the candela per square meter (the base unit). To convert A → B, multiply by A's factor and divide by B's:</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Unit</th><th>= this many candela per square meters</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        <tr><td>Candela per square meter / Nit (cd/m²)</td><td>1</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Kilocandela per square meter (kcd/m²)</td><td>1,000</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Stilb (sb)</td><td>10,000</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Candela per square foot (cd/ft²)</td><td>10.76391041671</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Candela per square inch (cd/in²)</td><td>1,550.0031000062</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Foot-lambert (fL)</td><td>3.426259099632</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Lambert (L)</td><td>3,183.098861837907</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Apostilb (asb)</td><td>0.318309886184</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>When you need it</h2>
      <p>Context: SDR monitors target 80–120 nits, phones peak above 2,000 nits outdoors, and SMPTE recommends ~48 nits (14 fL) for dark-room cinema. If a projector spec says lumens, that is total flux — luminance depends on screen size and gain.</p>

      <h2>Sources & methodology</h2>
      <p>Conversion factors follow <a href="https://www.nist.gov/pml/special-publication-811" rel="noopener" target="_blank">NIST Special Publication 811</a>; exact-by-definition factors are marked in the tool itself. All math runs client-side in your browser — nothing is uploaded.</p>

      <h2>More conversion guides</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/blog/illuminance-converter">How to convert lux to foot-candles</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/luminous-intensity-converter">How to convert mcd to candela and candlepower</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/screen-size-calculator">How to calculate TV and monitor dimensions from the diagonal</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Or browse everything at once in the <a href="/blog/new-unit-converters">new unit &amp; sizing converters roundup</a>.</p>

      <hr class="blog-divider" />
      <p class="blog-footer-note">The <a href="/luminance-converter">Luminance Converter</a> tool is free, runs locally, and never sends your data to a server. More <a href="/converter">converter tools</a> at <a href="/">maratool.com</a>.</p>
    </BlogPostShell>
  </Layout>
</Base>
